### Requests for the HTTP client built into Android Studio and IntelliJ IDEA.
### Start the server with `npm run dev`, then press the run icon next to a request.
### Locally the server accepts development tokens: "dev:alice" signs in as Alice.

@host = http://127.0.0.1:8787
@token = dev:alice

### The server and its database are up
GET {{host}}/health

### No token: 401 with WWW-Authenticate
GET {{host}}/v1/me

### My profile; the first request creates the account
GET {{host}}/v1/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Onboarding, step by step
PATCH {{host}}/v1/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "displayName": "Alice" }

###
PATCH {{host}}/v1/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "ageConfirmed": true, "acceptedTermsVersion": "2026-10-14", "marketingOptIn": false }

### Delete the account
DELETE {{host}}/v1/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Queue a generation (needs a finished onboarding). Reuse the key when retrying.
POST {{host}}/v1/tracks
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: attempt-0001

{ "prompt": "Dreamy synth-pop about a night drive through Kyiv, warm female vocals", "lengthMs": 30000 }

### Try an error screen: the mock rejects the prompt and suggests another one
POST {{host}}/v1/tracks
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: attempt-0002

{ "prompt": "A song exactly like a famous band [mock:bad_prompt]" }

### My tracks, newest first
GET {{host}}/v1/tracks?limit=20
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Generations left today
GET {{host}}/v1/me/quota
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
